// Host-boundary doctrine (ported from 0.3.x capture, stamped by the
// author 2026-08-20): a fiber switch may never cross a LIVE host call
// boundary -- the native's C frame cannot be parked or resumed. A
// boundary that opened and closed before the switch is fine.
//
// NEEDS a host that registers `reenter(fn)` (calls zym_callClosurev) --
// the test minihost provides it; the packed CLI does not.

// Legal: boundary closed before the switch.
var f = Fiber.new(func() {
    var x = reenter(func() { return 21 })
    Fiber.yield(x * 2)
    return x
})
assert(Fiber.call(f) == 42, "switch after boundary closed")
assert(Fiber.call(f) == 21, "completes")
print("fiber host-boundary legal shapes ok")
